# The chat panel this demo shows is published as a dev build of Stigmer's open-source main, and dev
# builds live only on Stigmer's own public npm store (no login). npm picks a registry per scope, not per
# package, so this one folder sends the whole @stigmer scope there; the rest of the repository keeps
# resolving @stigmer from npmjs.com, which is why this package has its own lockfile and is not a
# workspace member.
@stigmer:registry=https://us-central1-npm.pkg.dev/pc-stigmer-foundation/stigmer-npm/
